  "query_preview": "..\n(Sunday Night through next Saturday)\nIssued at 1102 AM CDT Sat Jul 25 2026\n\nCAMs are showing the potential for an MCS to ride the periphery of\nthe upper ridge into Middle Tennessee Sunday night into Monday\nmorning. The NBM has not caught onto this idea, but PoPs were\nadded to account for this. Monday and Tuesday look like the\nhottest days of the forecast with highs getting into the mid to\neven upper 90s. Afternoon heat indices will approach 110 degrees\nboth days west of the plateau. \n\nA surface front will move through our area late Tuesday as an\nupper trough digs out of the Great Lakes towards New England. Some\nshowers and storms can be expected ahead of this front. Along with\nsome rain chances the front will bring dew points back down to \nthe 60s and temperatures back closer to normal with highs in the \nmid 80s to around 90 degrees for the rest of the week. Behind the\nfront, rain chances will drop as well.",
